Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:48:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] ARM64: record baseline benchmark results

util-linux has no benchmark suite, so this records a small reproducible
one: hexdump -C on 8 MiB, rev on 200k lines, column -t on 50k rows, and
2000 look / 500 uuidgen -r / 500 getopt invocations. The ARM64 build
runs natively from an ARM64 MSYS userland. It is compared with the
official x86_64 MSYS2 util-linux 2.42.4 and with an x86_64 build of
this same tree, both under x64 emulation. Outputs match byte for byte
across all three.

The ARM64 build is 1.6-1.9x faster on the process-spawn workloads and
0.76-0.90x on the stream workloads (hexdump, rev, column).

Signed-off-by: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
