+util-linux 2.40.2 (MSYS2 recipe tree, branch arm64-port) - Windows ARM64 baseline benchmark
+=========================================================================================
+Host: Snapdragon(R) X Elite - X1E80100 - Qualcomm(R) Oryon(TM) CPU (SC8380XP), Windows 11 ARM64. Reps=5 per workload, wall clock, median reported.
+Configurations (run one after another on an otherwise idle host):
+  arm64     - this tree, aarch64-pc-cygwin -O2, build-arm64/dest/usr/bin, run natively from an ARM64 MSYS
+              userland (Git-for-Windows native ARM64 tree, msys-2.0.dll 3.6.10 aarch64)
+  x64-msys2 - official MSYS2 util-linux 2.42.4-1 in C:\msys64\usr\bin, x86_64 msys-2.0.dll 3.6.12,
+              run under Windows x64 emulation (Prism)
+  x64-same  - this same tree built natively by x86_64 MSYS2 with the same configure options and -O2,
+              run under x64 emulation (isolates the util-linux version difference)
+Workloads (deterministic inputs from gen-data.sh, awk srand seeds 42/7/3):
+  hexdump_C_8MiB     hexdump -C on an 8 MiB file
+  rev_200k_lines     rev on 200,000 lines (10 MB)
+  column_t_50k_rows  column -t on 50,000 rows x 5 columns
+  look_x2000         2,000 look invocations against a 200k-word sorted list (process-spawn bound)
+  uuidgen_r_x500     500 uuidgen -r invocations (process-spawn bound)
+  getopt_x500        500 getopt invocations with short+long options (process-spawn bound)
+Spawn-bound loops are driven by the bash of each configuration (ARM64 bash for arm64, emulated x64 bash for
+the x64 rows), so they measure the whole userland, not util-linux alone.
+out_md5 = md5 of the workload output (stream workloads) or of the result count (loop workloads); identical
+across all three configurations, so the outputs match byte for byte.
+
+Summary (median ms; ratio = x64 / arm64, >1 means ARM64 is faster)
+workload                  arm64  x64-msys2   x64-same  msys2/arm64   same/arm64
+hexdump_C_8MiB             4050       3098       3068         0.76         0.76
+rev_200k_lines             1783       1601       1369         0.90         0.77
+column_t_50k_rows           515        432        427         0.84         0.83
+look_x2000                33292      62856      57083         1.89         1.71
+uuidgen_r_x500             8736      15225      14244         1.74         1.63
+getopt_x500                8386      13893      14048         1.66         1.68
+
